    [scope_too_narrow] pre-test-failure-modes/defect-stage-not-invoked-for-all-derived-criteria
      `enumerate_defects()` only runs over obligations where `enumerable(o.type)` is true, so any derived criterion type that is not in that predicate gets no failure-mode note at all even though the criterion asks for each derived criterion.
      src/acceptance/defects/enumeration.py#0
      src/acceptance/defects/taxonomy.py#0
    [wrong_output_shape] pre-test-failure-modes/defect-empty-set-without-clear-note
      When an obligation has no plausible defects, the code stores an empty `DefectSet` with a reason string, but the report renders that as a special advisory block rather than a straightforward per-criterion failure-mode note, so the observable output shape can differ from the criterion's requested notes-per-criterion form.
      src/acceptance/defects/enumeration.py#0
      src/acceptance/report.py#1

  recorded-failure-fields
    [missing_case] recorded-failure-fields/missing-criterion-field
      The recorded failure entry can be written without the criterion it belongs to: `DefectSet` stores `obligation_id`, `defects`, `reason`, `obligation_text`, `carry_key`, `region_digests`, and `carried_from`, but there is no field that records the criterion classification/type for the set itself, so the review record does not carry all five required fields at the set level.
